5
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:28,416
With the known F one reward defect, the robot barely follows
that command. These are normal and

6
00:00:28,416 --> 00:00:31,548
faulty captures, not a before and after repair video.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,053
Now the application replays a separate, completed P P O
epoch failure. The public source files are

8
00:00:41,053 --> 00:00:46,394
hash verified. Both policies survive twenty seconds, but
linear tracking error rises from zero point

9
00:00:46,394 --> 00:00:50,666
one four six to one point one six nine meters per second.

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:59,035
The recorded Nemotron response first selects the reward
inspection. It returns normal. The following

11
00:00:59,035 --> 00:01:05,069
inspections use the registered sequence, rather than more
model choices. This matters: a plausible

12
00:01:05,069 --> 00:01:08,086
